<title>UK: BT-led group to bid for 1.5 bln stg UK award.</title>
<headline>BT-led group to bid for 1.5 bln stg UK award.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Telecommunications said on Thursday it formed a consortium with Motorola, Nokia and TRW Inc to bid for a 1.5 billion stg government contract to create a national emergency communications system in Britain.</p>
<p>The 15-year contract, known as the Public Safety Radio Communications Project, will be awarded by Britain's Home Office, BT said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;Driven by service and customer needs, the Home Office requirement calls for a radical improvement to the radio communications systems currently serving the emergency services in England, Wales and Scotland,&quot; the company said.</p>
<p>The BT-led consortium is called Quadrant, it added.</p>
<p>No date was given for the awarding of the contract.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
